    "description": "CTEST Laboratories is a non-profit research facility dedicated to the study and development of epistemological and hermeneutical systems based in software. Software systems that model logical deduction, abduction and induction form the basis of our work in the field of computational philosophy. We believe that the quality of life saving, life altering or mission criticial decisions can be enhanced by logic-based software. \n\nOur mission is to:\n\nDevelop working theories and models of software epistemology that define, explore, and advances the field of computational philosophy.\n\nInvestigate possibilities for enhancing the cognitive anatomy with logic systems that are based in computational epistemology.\n\nDiscover and develop epistemological methods that qualify and quantify the authority, consistency, rationality, and pedigree of complex information systems, artificial intelligent systems and applications of autonomous computational intelligence.\n\nAt Ctest Laboratories, my primary function is a software and visualization engineer. I am the primary developer of \"The M.I.N.D.\"  (Mental image and Neural Display). This is a visualization system of the inner processes and structures of our software components. MIND visualization system presents multiple views of the processing within a software component. The MIND has five levels of visualization:\n\n    Problem Solving\n    Internal Representations\n    Logical Representations and Models\n    Graphic/Textual User Interface\n    Anthropomorphic  \n\nAs a visualization engineer, I design and develop user interfaces. visual summaries, and visualization systems.",
