    "name": "Northeast Ohio ACM",
    "position": "Co-chair · Oct 2008 - Present",
    "dateRange": {},
    "description": "The NEOACM Professional Chapter is dedicated to advancing the art, science, engineering, and application of information technology, serving both professional and public interests by fostering the open interchange of information and by promoting the highest professional and ethical standards.\nCurrently, our focus for 2014 will be ROBOTICS, the biggest growing tech sector. It is a key economic enabler having the potential to transform U.S. society by developing new markets and industries, creating new jobs in manufacturing to software engineering, and addressing a number of issues of national importance. This year, 2014, the NEOACM will be supply our members and the professional community with information on conferences, articles, links to important websites, local businesses, and government initiatives having to do with this industry.\n\nWe are also sponsoring a ROBOTICS CHALLENGE. The primary goal of the NEOACM Robotics Challenge is to develop a team of robots that can work in small 3 to 5 agent groups. They are to perform forensic analysis in potentially dangerous/hazardous environments, threat assessments of unknown or unidentified substances, and to provide inferential assertions with respect to persons/articles of interest. If you are interested visit: www.neoacmchapter.org"
